  "question": {
    "text": "<p>Given are two statements one is labelled as Assertion and other is labelled as Reason.</p><p><strong>Assertion</strong>: Magnesium can reduce <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>Al</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math> at a temperature below <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1350</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#176;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math>, while above <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1350</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#176;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math> aluminium can reduce <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>MgO</mi></math>.</p><p><strong>Reason</strong>: The melting and boiling points of magnesium are lower than those of aluminium.</p><p>In light of the above statements, choose most appropriate answer from the options given below</p>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "md0KX",
      "text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct, and Reason is correct explanation of Assertion.",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "6DnVA",
      "text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct, but Reason is NOT the correct explanation of Assertion.",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "DlePY",
      "text": "Assertion is correct Reason is not correct.",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "qpMLc",
      "text": "Assertion is not correct, Reason is correct.",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/43ffce16-a115-460a-affc-7d80d97c1317-9709796.png\" style=\"width: 340px; height: 298px;\" /></p><table border=\"1\" cellpadding=\"1\" cellspacing=\"1\" style=\"width: 500px;\">\t<tbody>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td>&nbsp;</td>\t\t\t<td>Mg</td>\t\t\t<td>Al</td>\t\t</tr>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td>Melting point</td>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>924</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math></td>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>933</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math></td>\t\t</tr>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td>Boiling point</td>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1363</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math></td>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2740</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math></td>\t\t</tr>\t</tbody></table><p>it is true that magnesium (Mg) can reduce aluminium oxide&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi>Al</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;and aluminium can also reduce magnesium oxide. According to the Elingham diagram, we find that below&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mn>1350</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math>, Mg can reduce aluminium oxide and when the temperature is above&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mn>1350</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math>, Al can reduce magnesium oxide.</p><p>So,&nbsp;Both Assertion and Reason are correct, but Reason is NOT the correct explanation of Assertion.</p>",
    "image": null
  },
